## Feature → Repo Quick Map

| Feature area | Primary repo(s) |
|--------------|-----------------|
| NETCONF config / YANG RPC | `netconf-polt`, `xpon-yang` |
| ONU / OMCI / vOMCI | `netconf-polt/onu_mgmt`, `xpon-protos` |
| OLT chip / PON port / BAL | read `sw-bcm686olt`; code in `netconf-polt/balapi` |
| DHCP/PPPoE/protocol | `xpon-apps/protocol-handler` |
| System mgmt / events / metrics | `xpon-apps` |
| Shared infra (log, ipc, redis) | `xpon-libs` |
| gRPC / protobuf API | `xpon-protos` |
| YANG model only | `xpon-yang` |
| sysrepo/libyang behavior | read `sysrepo`, `libyang`; fix/integration in `netconf-polt` |

---

## Agent Behavior Summary

1. Receive feature → output **task breakdown** (design / code / review / compile).
2. Confirm **Oreo/** branch in each affected repo before editing.
3. **Never edit** `sw-bcm686olt`, `libyang`, or `sysrepo` — read-only for learning.
4. **Learn code style** from target module before editing; never edit read-only repos.
5. Implement minimal changes; add **DbgCli/DBC** commands when feature introduces inspectable runtime state.
6. Draft CR + commit message; run **module bitbake** for affected editable recipes only.
7. Report build result and verification steps (incl. DbgCli smoke test); escalate to `xpon-olt-bundle` only when integration testing requires full image.
